st Arabic translations, representing their earliest testimony: three lemmata from Aristotle’s &lt;i&gt;De Anima&lt;/i&gt; and one from Alexander of Aphrodisias’ &lt;i&gt;De Anima&lt;/i&gt; in Isḥāq ibn Ḥunayn’s (830-911) translations.</note></biblStruct><bibl type="formatted" subtype="bibliography" resp="https://www.zotero.org/styles/chicago-note-bibliography-17th-edition">
